        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"project-the-external-lorentz-indices\">Project the external Lorentz indices</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Color has already been averaged. For off-shell <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(p^2\\ne0||)</marimo-tex>, use\n$<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\mathcal P_{\\mu\\nu}=\n\\frac{1}{D-1}\n\\left(g_{\\mu\\nu}-\\frac{p_\\mu p_\\nu}{p^2}\\right).||)</marimo-tex>$\nIt extracts <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(p^2\\Pi_T||)</marimo-tex> from\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||((p^2g^{\\mu\\nu}-p^\\mu p^\\nu)\\Pi_T||)</marimo-tex>.\nThis replaces the default external polarization vectors; it is not an\nadditional polarization sum. The helper reads the actual external slots.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
